# The two names everything else derives from.
#
# Sourced by setup-ingress.sh, setup-turn.sh, verify-live.sh, farm-online.sh and farm-check.sh, so
# moving the farm to a domain is an edit HERE and nowhere else. Before this file existed the console
# hostname was hardcoded in seven places and the relay address in two, which meant a rename was nine
# edits and one of them would be missed.
#
# Committed on purpose: neither value is a secret, both are public DNS, and a checked-in default is
# what makes `farm-check.sh` work on a fresh clone without setup. Secrets live in deploy/secrets/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the console
# Serves the console, /v1, the WebDriver hub, and /dp (the live-view socket). Caddy terminates TLS
# here and it is the ONLY public listener on the control plane.
#
# `mfarm.dev` was registered 2026-08-20 through Cloud Domains; Cloud DNS (zone `mfarm-dev`) is
# authoritative, and this A record points at the reserved address `mfarm-lab-ip` (34.100.138.213 —
# the name is historically wrong, see below).
#
# The old name, `34-100-138-213.sslip.io`, still works: Caddy serves both during the transition, and
# sslip.io resolves the dashed form to that IP by construction. Retire it from the Caddyfile once
# everyone is on the new name.
MFARM_PUBLIC_HOST=farm.mfarm.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the media relay
# coturn on the CONTROL PLANE, since 2026-10-03 (ADR-0047) — it was on the device host, and down
# whenever that was. Points at the reserved address `mfarm-lab-ip` (34.100.138.213), the same as
# MFARM_PUBLIC_HOST: one machine, two names, because the relay is a different service on it.
#
# A NAME, not an IP, since the domain landed — and `setup-turn.sh` resolves it, because coturn's
# `external-ip` will not accept a hostname and a name there yields a server that starts cleanly and
# hands clients an address they cannot use.
MFARM_TURN_HOST=turn.mfarm.dev

# The device hosts' PRIVATE addresses: the only private addresses the relay may forward to, so a
# browser can reach a Cuttlefish device through it. Space-separated. A second device host adds its
# address here, and `setup-turn.sh` is re-run on the control plane (docs/SECOND_HOST.md).
MFARM_RELAY_PEERS=${MFARM_RELAY_PEERS:-10.160.0.2}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- naming, because it will confuse
# THE TWO RESERVED ADDRESSES ARE NAMED BACKWARDS, and it is not a mistake anyone can safely fix:
#
#   mfarm-lab-ip  34.100.138.213  ->  mfarm-cp   (the CONTROL PLANE)
#   mfarm-ip      34.100.159.34   ->  mfarm-lab  (the DEVICE HOST)
#
# Both names date from the single-box era. GCP cannot rename a reserved address — you release and
# re-reserve, and a release hands the address back to the pool where somebody else may take it. The
# console URL and its certificate both depend on 34.100.138.213 keeping that exact value, so the
# names stay wrong and this comment exists instead.
